nt :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402780} {:answer/id #uuid "341ee6bc-c870-5be4-a9af-153355b7a5a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0babb588-cb94-586c-9b9b-239ddf850608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402777} :answer-field/id #uuid "eba24bc4-353b-563d-b970-3c4e99c8ae95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402776}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a1fe1df-e314-527e-a884-f0c092b97472" :question/math-academy-id "q-42090" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b19292e-d665-566f-8c6f-7d83c4d69c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333545} {:answer/id #uuid "7039880d-285d-542d-8eed-1662170a86ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334012} {:answer/id #uuid "7de24423-58a1-5fc2-baf5-dde65d746a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334113} {:answer/id #uuid "ca309238-a2b3-5c28-8c7c-56e6c410616b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334750} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe722d3-8558-53eb-8a6e-850293b2db44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b19292e-d665-566f-8c6f-7d83c4d69c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333545} :answer-field/id #uuid "96649b7c-8415-520e-af03-f8b52df45dd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c8b870-01b8-5cdd-a0e6-31fdbbd32f0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-68740" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262604 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices